From 81256882d49a1df45e4e3ea7c53a7a2b0f665ee7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alie Jie Li <alisonjieli@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:42:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Work in progress: email-first sign-up, the confirmation page
 and the Get started funnel

A live probe on September 23, 2026 showed that a second sign-up link for an
address that is not confirmed keeps the first password, so whoever registers
an address first sets its password. The record is
artifacts/architecture-audit-2026-09-19/identity-unconfirmed-signup-probe-1.json.

Sign-up now takes the address alone (service_account_signup_request/v2); a
request with a password, and the retired version 1, is refused before
anything is counted. The service generates a random password for the
provider's link request and keeps it nowhere. The new /auth/confirm view
clears the token from the address, asks for a password first, and on submit
verifies the link, sets the password and only then opens the account.
Recovery uses the same page from a form on /login. The /signup form posts to
the service instead of the provider's own signUp and carries the release 21
consent sentence. Registration is reported open only where the service can
send the link. The session record names where paid access comes from, and a
new /get-started funnel shows five steps with one primary action per state,
telling an invited account that its invitation covers Baltor Pro.

Checked: account_email_checks 87 of 87, with a removed-guard control for each
new rule; observability_checks 45 of 45. Not yet run: the browser check with
its new journey block and controls, and the full CI set. Remaining work, the
live steps and the checks are in docs/verification/HANDOFF-signup-2026-09-23.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
